Question Title: Deployment Project Permissions

Question Link: https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/3wz3wv7c89fo?lecture_hash=vifkrugjcwth

Solution:
chmod 700 deployment/app/*.py
chmod 770 deployment/datasets deployment/datasets/*
chmod 644 deployment/docs/OVERVIEW.md
chmod 755 deployment/bin/*.sh

Approach:
1. Used the numeric form of chmod, where read = 4, write = 2 and execute = 1, and each digit stands for owner, group and others in that order.
2. For the Python files I wanted only the owner to have full access, so I used 700.
3. For datasets/ I gave owner and group full access and others none, so 770. I applied it to the directory and to the files inside it.
4. For OVERVIEW.md the owner reads and writes while group and others only read, so 644.
5. For the shell scripts everyone needs to run them but only the owner should edit them, so 755.
6. I ran the commands from outside deployment/, so every path starts with deployment/.